{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-cohomology-LC}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:41397613f4677d39c09bb74fe2e44472d81ea91b0f27cc6de3bc61d979d64e38", "source_text": "Cohomology on Hausdorff and locally quasi-compact spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c72df18c0ad52875a712b1777e21cf1619ee79e080299cfec4a898706f111ef", "unit_id": "tag:09WY:title"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{LC}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ee43cdb5c0497e635633b7b06c0353e992a9d077c6979f75acdf57b8b213cdc2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:98269a9769834477378ce02a78f00131f91c612c50ca3f368186054175d7b8d2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe continue our convention to say ``Hausdorff and locally quasi-compact''\ninstead of saying ``locally compact'' as is often done in the literature.\nLet <MATH_0001> denote the category whose objects are Hausdorff and\nlocally quasi-compact topological spaces and whose morphisms are continuous\nmaps.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b247c96091b5c1d0e35db12730a216626e7106f4a5e21745493923825f0cdbcf", "unit_id": "tag:09WY:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$Y$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\times_Z Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-LC-basic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:68d3d6022569c7caaf93bf269595821542f59dbd5ff667ded55356b0eb403261", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:98834f0874d96215888aa197afd25d9e3694857f5a94174daa705d8de82fc935", "source_text": "The category <MATH_0001> has fibre products and a final object and hence\nhas arbitrary finite limits. Given morphisms <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003>\nin <MATH_0004> with\n<MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> quasi-compact, then <MATH_0007> is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:252a8096f75d7f469e982acf16a0d94933c07492638d51a5432a7f089384c617", "unit_id": "tag:09WZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0002": "$Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\times_Z Y$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\times Y$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\times_Z Y$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\times Y$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$Y$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\times Y$", "MATH_0011": "$X \\times_Z Y$", "MATH_0012": "$X \\times Y$", "MATH_0013": "$X \\times_Z Y$", "MATH_0014": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0015": "$y \\in Y$", "MATH_0016": "$x \\in E \\subset X$", "MATH_0017": "$y \\in F \\subset Y$", "MATH_0018": "$E \\times_Z F$", "MATH_0019": "$(x, y)$", "MATH_0020": "$X \\times_Z Y$", "MATH_0021": "$\\textit{LC}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-section-Hausdorff}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-theorem-tychonov}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topology-lemma-fibre-product-closed}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{topology-lemma-closed-in-quasi-compact}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{topology-lemma-locally-quasi-compact-Hausdorff}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5690455408e25742fbb131f7852ebed9349f446c5cb3d6650641585322f30f5d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f24b589edbcd0091afbe13febe8c7d15bfa93d86a6076ac1d4bde12407180656", "source_text": "The final object is the singleton space. Given morphisms <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003> the fibre product <MATH_0004> is\na subspace of <MATH_0005>. Hence <MATH_0006> is Hausdorff as\n<MATH_0007> is Hausdorff by\nTopology, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nIf <MATH_0008> and <MATH_0009> are quasi-compact, then <MATH_0010> is quasi-compact by \nTopology, Theorem <REF_0002>.\nSince <MATH_0011> is a closed subset of <MATH_0012>\n(Topology, Lemma <REF_0003>)\nwe find that <MATH_0013> is quasi-compact by\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0004>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nFinally, returning to the general case, if <MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015>\nwe can pick quasi-compact neighbourhoods <MATH_0016> and\n<MATH_0017> and we find that <MATH_0018> is a quasi-compact\nneighbourhood of <MATH_0019> by the result above. Thus <MATH_0020>\nis an object of <MATH_0021> by\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1dc320e966d0846da58e9adb0edb8a611366c2ef77c591793b4680e549092a8c", "unit_id": "tag:09WZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{LC}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ee43cdb5c0497e635633b7b06c0353e992a9d077c6979f75acdf57b8b213cdc2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:98269a9769834477378ce02a78f00131f91c612c50ca3f368186054175d7b8d2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can endow <MATH_0001> with a stronger topology than the usual one.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c315fa787d916d507ca5ad083665fc514d5e5c2307f299fbdf3b667eae09b77f", "unit_id": "tag:09WY:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$i_1, \\ldots, i_n \\in I$", "MATH_0005": "$E_j \\subset X_{i_j}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\bigcup f_{i_j}(E_j)$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-covering-LC}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c67d91e4b9cdce7e002136acdc2f21b55391633cc8399c16e85e76e93a5af410", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d1d8870f02dcc87c8b82a5afb69567c77cf7d9b5d4dbd014a9521d3e3cbbfedd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a family of morphisms with fixed target\nin the category <MATH_0002>. We say this family is a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>qc covering<TEXTITCLOSE_0001><FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>This is nonstandard notation.\nWe chose it to remind the reader of fpqc coverings of schemes.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>\nif for every <MATH_0003> there exist <MATH_0004> and\nquasi-compact subsets <MATH_0005> such that\n<MATH_0006> is a neighbourhood of <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:78691bd1096552bb878a61fb341c9fa0b3f1aa6cd3b3a7fc85672ac6009f6d0f", "unit_id": "tag:09X0:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{U_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:287588917e7d4217dce1884e3b231661e4d457ffd7e677d32fb87291568aed1b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e3349522a8973a8e19418c1108546a438ed29a4da2c0a4f86dd02e602def8aa2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nObserve that an open covering <MATH_0001> of an object of <MATH_0002>\ngives a qc covering <MATH_0003> because <MATH_0004> is locally quasi-compact.\nWe start with the obligatory lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95a1d78a3df11024856bc3e6341610045b6bd06d3f71eb33c73dc8210ce12ac0", "unit_id": "tag:09WY:prose-0003"}
